# Windows clones default to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites every checked-out
# text file to CRLF. That is fine for the docs, and fatal for anything a Linux
# shell has to parse — WSL students got a repo whose scripts could not even be
# read:
#
#   setup.sh: line 23: syntax error near unexpected token `$'do\r''
#   setup.sh: line 4: set: pipefail: invalid option name
#
# So pin LF for everything that is executed rather than read. Same file, both
# host OSes; Windows editors have handled LF for a decade.
*.sh        text eol=lf
Makefile    text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.ini       text eol=lf
